        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Gd(NO3)3·6H2O was mixed with pivalic acid (HO2CtBu), tert-butylphosphonic acid (H2O3PtBu) and isopropylamine (iPrNH2) in isobutyl alcohol (iBuOH) in the mole ratio 1 : 14 : 0.8 : 1. The solution was refluxed for 3 h. After cooling to room temperature, crystals of 1 formed after four days (yield 50–60%). The same shared procedure was used for the isostructural Ln8 series (Ln = Gd, Tb, Dy).",
